sequenceDiagram
    participant C1 as Caller 1 (starts the load)
    participant C2 as Caller 2 (joins the load)
    participant C3 as Caller N (joins the load)
    participant R as Redis

    Note over C1,C3: All request same key — cache miss in this process

    C1->>R: GET key
    C2->>R: GET key
    C3->>R: GET key
    R-->>C1: miss (nil)
    R-->>C2: miss (nil)
    R-->>C3: miss (nil)

    Note over C1,C3: singleflight: the first caller starts the load, the rest wait on it
    C1->>C1: start load (detached from caller ctx, bounded by LoadTimeout)

    C1->>R: GET key (double-check, another process may have stored it)
    R-->>C1: miss (nil)
    C1->>C1: fn() — compute value (DB query / API call)
    C1->>R: SET key value (TTL ± 10%)
    C1-->>C2: shared result
    C1-->>C3: shared result

    Note over C1,C3: Caller ctx cancelled: that caller returns ctx.Err(), the load continues.
    Note over C1,C3: Redis read error counts as a miss; Redis write error still returns the value. Both go to OnError.
    Note over C1,C3: All 3 callers get result. fn() called once in this process.
